<h3>10.4 Quality pre-flight evidence</h3>
<p>The delivered report is checked by the companion report tests. Their scope is numerical consistency, literal hand anchors, calculation-source freshness, output encoding, local references and report structure; those checks do not establish engineering acceptance.</p>
<p>Replacement and maintenance are checked separately against the public examples. Displayed headline values are recalculated from the displayed inputs. The chart values are calculated by the module, without a browser-side cost formula. Source digests cover the calculation files only and are embedded in the document data.</p>
<p>Test results and checks attempted for the delivered revision are stated with the accompanying change description. The rebuild command is provided in <a href="#s9-2">Section 9.2</a>.</p>
